The error occurs because `Fw/Com/ComTypes.hpp` is not a standard F Prime header. The correct header for `Fw::ComPacketType` is `Fw/Com/ComPacket.hpp`. Here's the corrected test:

```cpp tester
#include "Fw/Com/ComPacket.hpp"

void FprimeRouterTester::testBufferNotFoundInContextTable() {
    REQUIREMENT("SVC-ROUTER-009");
    // Test that returning a buffer not found in the context table emits the BufferContextNotFound event
    // and returns the buffer with an empty context.
    U8 data[1];
    Fw::Buffer buffer(data, sizeof(data));
    this->clearHistory();
    this->invoke_to_fileBufferReturnIn(0, buffer);
    ASSERT_from_dataReturnOut_SIZE(1);  // buffer should be returned via dataReturnOut
    ASSERT_EQ(this->fromPortHistory_dataReturnOut->at(0).data.getData(), data);
    ASSERT_EQ(this->fromPortHistory_dataReturnOut->at(0).data.getSize(), sizeof(data));
    ASSERT_EVENTS_BufferContextNotFound_SIZE(1);  // event should be emitted
    ComCfg::FrameContext defaultCtx;
    ASSERT_EQ(this->fromPortHistory_dataReturnOut->at(0).context.get_vcId(), defaultCtx.get_vcId());
}
```

```cpp main
TEST(FprimeRouter, TestBufferNotFoundInContextTable) {
    COMMENT("Return a buffer not found in the context table emits BufferContextNotFound and returns empty context");
    Svc::FprimeRouterTester tester;
    tester.testBufferNotFoundInContextTable();
}
```

The fix was to replace the incorrect `#include "Fw/Com/ComTypes.hpp"` with the correct `#include "Fw/Com/ComPacket.hpp"`. The test now properly verifies requirement SVC-ROUTER-009 by:
1. Creating a buffer that was never handed off (so it won't be in the context table)
2. Returning it via `fileBufferReturnIn`
3. Verifying the `BufferContextNotFound` event was emitted
4. Verifying the buffer was returned with an empty context (default vcId)
